  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMLN computes CRT ln(IMABS(z)) + atan2(im, re) i and returns #NUM! at 0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMLN(inumber) returns #NUM! when IMABS(inumber) = 0, and otherwise formats crt_log(crt_hypot(re, im)) + crt_atan2(im, re) i with Excel's 15-digit complex text formatter. Unlike IMARGUMENT (which computes atan(im/re) and returns #DIV/0! on ratio overflow), IMLN uses atan2(im, re). All 1,209 full-bank IMLN rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imln.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (prefix_metadata row 122); 1,209/1,209 full-bank rows match.",
